-- title:
--   Hecke algebra realises all q-coefficients through a₁
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let $n$ be a nonzero natural number. The assertion is that there exists an operator $t$ lying in [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra p 2 ∅`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), that is, in the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}\bigl(S_2(\Gamma_0(p))\bigr)$ generated by the set `heckeGenerators p 2 ∅`, which consists of the operators `heckeTLin 2 hℓ hℓN` for all primes $\ell$ not dividing $p$ together with the operators `heckeULin 2 hqN` for all primes $q$ dividing $p$ (the excluded set being empty, no generator is omitted), such that for every cusp form $f$ of weight $2$ for $\Gamma_0(p)$ one has $$\mathrm{qCoeff}(t\,f)(1) = \mathrm{qCoeff}(f)(n),$$ i.e. the first coefficient of the $q$-expansion at $\infty$ of $t\,f$ equals the $n$-th coefficient of the $q$-expansion of $f$. Here the weight is the integer $2$ and [`ModularFormClass.qCoeff`](def/FLTPrelim_Modularity.html#L19) denotes the coefficients of the $q$-expansion at the cusp $\infty$. The operator $t$ is asserted to exist uniformly in $f$, but no formula for it and no uniqueness are claimed.
--
--   This is the classical statement $a_n(f) = a_1(T_n f)$ (Diamond–Shurman, Proposition 5.3.1), in the form needed when the Hecke algebra is presented by its prime-index generators $T_\ell$ ($\ell \nmid p$) and $U_q$ ($q \mid p$). It is the input showing that the pairing $(t,f) \mapsto a_1(t f)$ between the weight-two Hecke algebra of $\Gamma_0(p)$ and $S_2(\Gamma_0(p))$ detects all $q$-coefficients, and it is used in the construction of $q$-integral structures and of Eisenstein-type eigenvectors modulo a prime.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CuspForm_exists_mem_heckeAlgebra_qCoeff_apply_one_eq.lean

import Definitions.Def_ModularForm_HeckeOperatorForms
import Definitions.Def_CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

theorem CuspForm.exists_mem_heckeAlgebra_qCoeff_apply_one_eq (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime] (n : ℕ) (hn : n ≠ 0) : ∃ t ∈ CuspForm.heckeAlgebra p 2 ∅, ∀ f : CuspForm (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 p) 2, ModularFormClass.qCoeff (t f) 1 = ModularFormClass.qCoeff f n := by sorry
